WEBVTT

00:00:00.530 --> 00:00:04.600
Operating near structures increases collision, turbulence, navigation, signal,

00:00:04.600 --> 00:00:06.000
and visual-occlusion risk.

00:00:06.000 --> 00:00:11.000
Maintain safe standoff, simple escape paths, visual awareness, and conservative speed.

00:00:11.000 --> 00:00:15.220
Do not enter spaces or fly beneath structures without specific authorization, capability,

00:00:15.220 --> 00:00:16.000
and procedures.

00:00:16.000 --> 00:00:20.220
Power lines and energized equipment can be difficult to see and may create serious

00:00:20.220 --> 00:00:20.510
electrical,

00:00:20.510 --> 00:00:23.000
electromagnetic, or operational hazards.

00:00:23.000 --> 00:00:26.000
Coordinate with the asset owner and use their required boundaries.

00:00:26.000 --> 00:00:29.950
A zoom lens is safer than unnecessary proximity.

00:00:29.950 --> 00:00:32.915
Control exposure to people and vehicles through scheduling, barriers, observers,

00:00:32.915 --> 00:00:34.000
site escorts, and route design.

00:00:34.000 --> 00:00:37.780
Stop when unbriefed activity enters the operating area or the crew can no longer maintain

00:00:37.780 --> 00:00:39.000
required separation.

00:00:39.000 --> 00:00:43.925
Sensitive sites may restrict imagery, radio use, mapping, cloud processing, storage,

00:00:43.925 --> 00:00:44.870
or disclosure.

00:00:44.870 --> 00:00:46.980
Confirm requirements before arrival.

00:00:46.980 --> 00:00:51.155
Protect credentials, firmware, controllers, networks, media, and inspection systems.

00:00:51.155 --> 00:00:53.000
Collect only scoped asset evidence.

00:00:53.000 --> 00:00:56.000
Avoid unrelated homes, people, security features, or operations.

00:00:56.000 --> 00:01:00.175
Limit access and retention, and document purpose and authorization.

00:01:00.175 --> 00:01:02.000
Inspection is not permission for surveillance.

00:01:02.000 --> 00:01:05.955
Abort criteria include weather deterioration, signal or navigation uncertainty,

00:01:05.955 --> 00:01:10.000
aircraft warnings, obstacle conflict, people or vehicles entering the area,

00:01:10.000 --> 00:01:13.915
privacy concerns, lost communication, or poor data quality.

00:01:13.915 --> 00:01:15.986
Safe recovery takes priority over completing coverage.

00:01:15.986 --> 00:01:21.540
At critical sites, coordinate radio use, cybersecurity, photography restrictions, escorts,

00:01:21.540 --> 00:01:23.970
emergency procedures, and data transfer with the owner.

00:01:23.970 --> 00:01:27.375
Do not assume an aviation approval overrides industrial, security,

00:01:27.375 --> 00:01:29.000
or process-safety controls.
